#### Interfaces

##### `Gadget`

A pocket-sized interface exercising the object surface

Passed as an **object pointer** (`i32`), wrapped by a JS class holding one reference. Constructors return an owned reference; methods lend the pointer as the implicit leading `self` argument; `close()` (or `Symbol.dispose`) releases the reference via the destroy symbol exactly once.

##### `weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_new`

Create a gadget with the given id

`weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_new(id: i64) -> i32`

| Param | API Type | Wasm | Notes |
|-------|----------|------|-------|
| `id` | `i64` | `i64` | native Wasm i64 |
| _returns_ | `Gadget` | `i32` | borrowed object pointer |

##### `weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_describe`

Render the gadget as a human-readable string

`weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_describe() -> i32`

| Param | API Type | Wasm | Notes |
|-------|----------|------|-------|
| _returns_ | `string` | `i32` | NUL-terminated C string pointer |

