##### `weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_clone`

Returns a second reference to the same object. Used when the wrapper is encoded as an object token inside a value buffer.

##### `weaveffi_kitchen_Gadget_destroy`

Releases one object reference. Called by the wrapper's `close()` (and by the finalizer backstop).

#### Callback Interfaces

##### `ReadyListener`

Consumer-implemented observer of ready items

Implemented in JS as an object with the methods below. Passed as an `i32` context key plus an `i32` pointer to the static `weaveffi_kitchen_ReadyListener_vtable` vtable; the vtable's trailing `free(ctx)` entry releases the JS object.

| Method | Parameters | Returns |
|--------|------------|---------|
| `onReady` | `code: number`, `msg: string` | `void` |
| `onItem` | `item: Item`, `gadget: Gadget` | `boolean` |

#### Structs

##### `Item`

Kitchen sink struct exercising every field feature

A plain JS object, serialized in a value buffer (`i32` ptr + `i32` len) at the boundary. Fields in declaration (wire) order:

| Field | Type |
|-------|------|
| `id` | `i64` |
| `name` | `string` |
| `count` | `i32` |
| `enabled` | `bool` |
| `ratio` | `f64` |
| `nick` | `u32` |
| `payload` | `bytes` |
| `tags` | `[string]` |
| `attrs` | `{string:string}` |
| `parent` | `i64?` |
| `token` | `Token` |
| `priority` | `Priority` |
| `gadget` | `Gadget?` |

#### Enums

##### `Priority`

Task priority levels

Passed as `i32` discriminant.

| Variant | Value |
|---------|-------|
| `Low` | `0` |
| `Normal` | `1` |
| `High` | `2` |

